  title="How to do a systematic literature review, step by step"
  description="The steps of a systematic literature review: protocol, search, two-stage screening, snowballing, data extraction, synthesis and the PRISMA flow diagram."
  question="How do you do a systematic literature review?"
  answer="Define a focused question, write and ideally register a protocol, then search several databases with a documented query. Remove duplicates, screen titles and abstracts against your criteria, then screen full texts and record a reason for every exclusion. Snowball through the references of included papers, extract data in a fixed form, appraise quality, synthesise the findings, and report the counts at each stage in a PRISMA flow diagram."
